From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 20:30:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 183/342] Remote Control: profiles for one application

A profile can be for one application ("Use while: <application> is
active"): its buttons count while that application is active, before those
of the profiles for any application. So the same remote does MediaPlayer's
keys in MediaPlayer and a music player's in that player, without
choosing a profile.
Profile files are version 3 (an "application" field); earlier ones are for
any application. The add-on asks the roster for the active application at
each new press; a held button repeats by its code, as it started. The
MediaPlayer and music player keystroke templates make an empty profile one for
their application; the Test button presses as if the profile's
application were active.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
